// src/kernel/core/syscall/handlers/sys_sched_yield.pdx — Wave κ (κ-01)
//
// sys_sched_yield() -> 0. SC+ sysno 24.
//
// Voluntary CPU release (POSIX sched_yield(2)). Calls sched_pick_next_r15
// to obtain the next runnable task on this CPU, and if the picker returns a
// task other than the current one, hands control to sched_switch_r15(next).
// If the picker returns the current task (nothing else runnable — a single
// affinity-eligible task, or the whole runqueue drained to idle-only), the
// syscall is a no-op and returns 0 without switching.
//
// The sysno was reserved at the SC+ freeze (24) as the classical
// SYS_SCHED_YIELD slot; kernel/core/sched/yield.pdx has a Phase-4/R10 stub
// (Yield.sched_yield) that always returned YIELD_OK without touching the
// runqueue, and until this landing there was no ring-3 caller path into
// even that stub. This file is the ring-3 body wired at sysno 24 in
// core/syscall/dispatch.pdx.
//
// Contract (SysV, 0 args):
//   -> rax = 0 unconditionally (POSIX sched_yield(2) never fails). No
//   errno path — even a fully-empty runqueue picks this CPU's idle TCB
//   via sched_pick_next_r15's pick_empty branch, and the je-self short-
//   circuit below then reads that as "self selected, no switch" and
//   returns 0. Callers use sched_yield as a fairness hint, not a
//   guarantee that another task runs.
//
// Alignment:
//   Entry rsp%16==8 (dispatch shim's `sub rsp,8` pad before `call`,
//   matching every other body in this directory). One push (rbx) lands
//   rsp%16==0 — exactly what the two nested calls (sched_pick_next_r15,
//   sched_switch_r15) both need. No additional pad required.
//
// Register discipline:
//   rbx = current TCB VA (callee-save, survives sched_pick_next_r15's
//   callee-save-clean contract — see pick_next.pdx L160 justification
//   which pins "Callee-save clean — no rbx/rbp/r12-r15 write anywhere
//   in the body").
//   rax = pick result (caller-save scratch).
//   rdi = sched_switch_r15's next_tcb arg (loaded from rax pre-call).
//
// Effects mem+sysreg, capabilities {sched}: mem transitive from
// sched_pick_next_r15's CB reads + sched_switch_r15's TCB reads/writes;
// sysreg transitive from sched_pick_next_r15's rdmsr IA32_GS_BASE +
// sched_switch_r15's xsave path. {sched} transitive from both callees.
//
// Audit: design/kernel/r17-m0-671-sys-execve-shim.md §Wave κ addendum.

module SysSchedYield = structure {
  pub let sys_sched_yield_body : () -> u64 !{mem, sysreg} @{sched} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem, sysreg},
      capabilities: {sched},
      justification: "Wave κ (κ-01): sys_sched_yield real body at SC+ sysno 24. Voluntary CPU release. Sequence: (1) push rbx (entry rsp%16==8 -> 0 for the two nested calls). (2) rbx = _current_tcb (baseline for the pick-returned-self short-circuit below). (3) call sched_pick_next_r15 -> rax = next runnable task on this CPU (may be this CPU's own idle TCB via pick_next's pick_empty branch if the runqueue is drained, or the current task itself under head-rotation semantics if it is the only affinity-eligible entry). (4) cmp rax, rbx: if picker returned self (single-eligible or drained-to-idle-and-current-is-idle), skip the switch — a self-yield is a no-op, not an infinite recursion into sched_switch_r15's own is-same-tcb assumption. (5) mov rdi, rax; call sched_switch_r15 — hand the CPU to the picked task. Control returns here when this task is switched back to. (6) xor rax, rax; pop rbx; ret — POSIX sched_yield(2) never fails, always returns 0. Register discipline: rbx (callee-save, one push, holds current TCB across sched_pick_next_r15 whose L160 justification pins 'no rbx/rbp/r12-r15 write anywhere in the body'); rax caller-save (pick result then return value); rdi caller-save (sched_switch_r15's next_tcb arg). Alignment: entry rsp%16==8, one push lands 0 for both nested calls. Effects {mem,sysreg}: mem transitive from pick_next's CB reads + switch's TCB reads/writes; sysreg transitive from pick_next's rdmsr IA32_GS_BASE + switch's xsave path. Capability {sched}: transitive from both callees. Labels prefixed ssy_.",
      block: {
        push rbx;                              // entry rsp%16==8 -> 0

        mov rax, [rip + _current_tcb];
        mov rbx, rax;                          // rbx = current TCB (survives pick)

        call sched_pick_next_r15;              // rax = next (or idle, or self)

        cmp rax, rbx;
        je  ssy_no_switch;                     // self-selected: no-op yield

        mov rdi, rax;                          // rdi = next_tcb
        call sched_switch_r15;                 // switch; returns when resumed

      ssy_no_switch:
        xor rax, rax;                          // POSIX sched_yield(2) returns 0
        pop rbx;
        ret
      }
    }
}
